  "tuning_disclosure": {
    "rusteda": "The RustEDA arm is the producer behind the published SKY130A row: its repair plans (measured-load buffers, five setup rewires, native diode and SS selection, grouped jumpers, horizontal V3 offsets) were developed over the recorded SKY130 trials against the shared gates' power, area, Fmax and antenna counts, not against LibreLane's runtime.",
    "librelane": "The published SKY130A LibreLane configuration uses LibreLane's defaults for antenna repair and post-GRT resizer margins. This plan screens it against the closure settings of the IHP recipe (antenna margin 50 with 6/4 iterations; resizer setup and hold margins 1.0/0.2 ns with full TNS repair) and against jumper-only antenna repair after detailed routing, the knob classes of the IHP screen, under the same selection rule and gates. Geometry, floorplan, density, padding and CTS knobs stay as published.",
    "harness": "LibreLane runs with TMPDIR=/tmp (tmpfs), where the published SKY130A and GF180MCU D runs kept Yosys's ABC temporary files. With TMPDIR on the ext4 /home volume, Yosys 0.70's parallel ABC mapping hung in synthesis in 3 of 3 runs (2026-11-17); with /tmp it finished in 92 s with the published synthesis netlist. Yosys also writes a merged-Liberty cache there under a new key in every run (as in the published run), so no sample reuses another's."
  },
